"""Storyboard source for P5, the four-stroke engine (v1, 2026-11-25).
build_scenes.py turns this into scenes.json, timing every scene from the narration's word timestamps.
Anchors are the first words of the scene's narration, lowercase, as spoken in script/narration.txt.

Format: one cycle in slow motion. A real-time clock and crank-angle dial sit top right in EVERY scene (look.md section 3) except where noted;
CHAPTERS below says what they show over time, build_scenes.py interpolates `clock_start` / `clock_end` (crank degrees) into scenes.json.

Tools: "motion-canvas" (2D), "blender" (3D hero; `clip` names one clip of scenes/blender/e1_engine.py: intake, compression, power, exhaust,
flame, crank), "archival" (public-domain still from research/assets.json shown in a chalk frame with a credit line; the portrait/drawing is
prepared by the asset step, ids from assets.md: I1 Otto portrait, P1 Otto patent US 194,047 sheet 2).
Heroes (showrunner ruling 2026-11-25): H1 cutaway (4 stroke clips, also the frozen still under every 2D aside), H2 flame front, H3 four-throw crank.

Colour meanings (look.md): chalk = structure; heat/orange = flame, hot gas, the bill; lime = the spark only; violet (refrigerant token) = the
air-fuel charge; muted = coasting strokes, stored momentum, inactive parts. Arrowheads only for heat. Max 7 words of on-screen text at once.
Michael's standing notes: hook on the viewer (S00a-S00g, our own animation, no photo), 1 s beat after the first line (S00a holds the lamp through it),
soft landing into the intro sting after S00g, nothing static over 8 s, every named person gets a who-they-were card (Otto, Langen, Beau de Rochas;
MIT, Mazda and the US DOE are organisations), Beau de Rochas name card only (no portrait).
"""

# (name, first scene id, last scene id, crank degrees at the start, at the end). Outside a chapter the clock holds at the last value.
# `spark` is a zoom-in on the last 30 degrees of compression: the dial hand holds at 360 (0.086 s) and a replay cursor moves inside the zoom (see S36 note).
CHAPTERS = [
    ("cold open and set-up", "S00a", "S06", 0, 0),
    ("intake", "S07", "S16", 0, 180),
    ("compression", "S17", "S33", 180, 360),
    ("spark replay", "S34", "S44", 360, 360),
    ("power", "S45", "S55", 360, 540),
    ("clock stopped", "S56", "S67", 540, 540),
    ("exhaust", "S68", "S77", 540, 720),
    ("close", "S78", "S83", 720, 720),
]


def sc(id, beat, anchor, tool, visual, changes, text, facts, **kw):
    return dict(id=id, beat=beat, anchor=anchor, tool=tool, visual=visual, changes=changes, text=text, facts=facts, **kw)


